.TH focusforge-cli-hot-pixels 1  "hot-pixels 0.2.1" 
.SH NAME
focusforge\-cli\-hot\-pixels \- Find hot pixels: pixels that differ from their neighbours at the same sensor position in more than half the frames. Frames are read as they are, without alignment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfocusforge\-cli hot\-pixels\fR [\fB\-\-set\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDIR\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find hot pixels: pixels that differ from their neighbours at the same sensor position in more than half the frames. Frames are read as they are, without alignment
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fI<KEY=VALUE>\fR
Set a parameter: `\-\-set key=value`, repeatable. A repeated key is last\-wins
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the count and the sensor coordinates as one JSON object
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log detail (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Log errors only
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIDIR\fR>
Directory of frames to search (non\-recursive, descending into a `frames` subdirectory)
.SH EXTRA
Parameters (\-\-set KEY=VALUE):
  hot\-pixel\-threshold Hot pixel threshold (default 7, 2 to 50)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.1
